{
  "raw": {
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22679": {
      "title": "Instructor, Interior Design, non-tenure-track, 1-year Appointment",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Instructor, Interior Design, non-tenure-track, 1-year Appointment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Instructor, Interior Design, non-tenure-track, 1-year Appointment Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested individuals are encouraged to submit their credentials as soon as possible for full consideration. Complete applications should be submitted by November 6 and should include: A letter of teaching application addressing interest in and qualifications for the position, as well as teaching philosophy A current curriculum vitae Transcript and evidence of highest degree achieved (unofficial transcripts accepted upon application, but official transcripts required at the time of hire) Evidence of teaching excellence and up to 20 images of student work with descriptions for each (PDF) Evidence of the candidate's creative or scholarly work in a portfolio (PDF) The names, emails, and phone numbers for 3 references. All applications and nominations will be immediately reviewed and handled in confidence. If you should have any questions, please contact: Jason Tselentis Department Chair tselentisj@winthrop.edu Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Instructor, Interior Design, non-tenure-track, 1-year Appointment Job Description Winthrop University announces a search for an Instructor of Interior Design. This is a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure-track appointment in the Department of Design. Our campus is located in Rock Hill (South Carolina) a short 30 minutes from Charlotte (North Carolina). Winthrop University seeks an experienced interior designer and/or architect with a degree in their field, and a proven record of relevant professional experience. We are seeking a candidate who is committed to student success, impact, and access, by fostering an environment that prioritizes inclusive excellence. Position Responsibilities This position requires in person, daily contact with students, faculty, staff and community, both on campus and in our downtown Design Center which is just a short walk away Teach 3–4 classes per semester Teach all levels in the undergraduate Bachelor of Design in Interior Design degree program Advise and mentor undergraduate Interior Design majors in professional and career preparation Participate in curriculum development, accreditation, assessment, and course planning Maintain creative and scholarly activity Fully support and participate in the department’s recruitment efforts Engage in professional service to the department, college, university, discipline, and community Seek and maintain relationships with community and industry partners to support student internships, applied design projects, and our programs Assume other responsibilities according to departmental needs and candidate’s qualifications About the College To learn more about the College of Visual & Performing Arts please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cvpa/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits At Winthrop University, we are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package that significantly enhances the total compensation for our employees. In partnership with the State of South Carolina and the Public Employee Benefit Authority ( PEBA ), our benefits include health and life insurance, generous paid leave, parental leave, and retirement programs. These benefits reflect our commitment to supporting the well-being and financial security of our employees. For more information please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/hr/employee-benefits.aspx Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/27/2026 Required Qualifications Candidates should hold a terminal degree in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, or Architecture. Candidates holding a bachelor’s degree within these disciplines, with significant teaching and professional experience deemed equivalent to a terminal degree may be considered Proficiency with industry-standard software (e.g. AutoCAD, Revit, SketchUp, and/or Bluebeam), as well as experience creating contract documentation using 3D software Record of teaching, scholarship, and professional activity Evidence of teaching excellence Willingness to collaborate, communicate, and contribute to the growth of the department Preferred Qualifications National Council for Interior Design Qualification ( NCIDQ ) certification or eligibility to pass the NCIDQ exam Minimally, three to five years professional practice in Interior Design, Architecture, or a closely related professional field Two years of university-level teaching experience Technology Integration such as Building Information Modeling ( BIM ), virtual reality (VR), or other digital tools that enhance the design process Awareness of and ability to teach Environmentally Conscious Design Employment Conditions Position is full-time, non-tenure-track, and salary is commensurate with qualifications. Application Instructions Interested individuals are encouraged to submit their credentials as soon as possible for full consideration. Complete applications should be submitted by November 6 and should include: A letter of teaching application addressing interest in and qualifications for the position, as well as teaching philosophy A current curriculum vitae Transcript and evidence of highest degree achieved (unofficial transcripts accepted upon application, but official transcripts required at the time of hire) Evidence of teaching excellence and up to 20 images of student work with descriptions for each ( PDF ) Evidence of the candidate’s creative or scholarly work in a portfolio ( PDF ) The names, emails, and phone numbers for 3 references. All applications and nominations will be immediately reviewed and handled in confidence. If you should have any questions, please contact: Jason Tselentis Department Chair tselentisj@winthrop.edu Open Date 08/27/2026 Application Review Date 08/27/2026 Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0010P PositionType: Faculty Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Faculty-Letter of application and statement of teaching philosophy Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All graduate transcripts Faculty-Evidence of teaching excellence Portfolio Faculty - List of References Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22696": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Administrative Assistant State Title Administrative Assistant State Class Code AA75 State Pay Table GEN Annual Salary/Hiring Range $30,600; Aug. 16 to May 15 each year. Job Purpose Reporting to the Administrative Coordinator, the Administrative Assistant provides administrative and operational support across the College of Business & Technology ( CBT ). Incumbent supports efficient office operations, including scheduling, student engagement activities, event logistics, tutoring operations, and routine personnel and communication functions, and serves as primary customer service contact for students, faculty, staff and visitors. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree; associate’s degree and two years of administrative support experience; or high school diploma and four years of administrative support experience. Proficiency with Microsoft 365. Preferred Qualifications Experience providing support in a higher education or academic environment. Experience coordinating events and student services activities. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Summary Knowledge of office management policies, procedures and best practices. Exceptional organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple tasks while maintaining attention to detail and meeting deadlines. Exceptional customer service skills. Effective oral and written communication skills. Ability to contribute to a positive, cooperative and professional environment. Effective interpersonal skills and the ability to establish and maintain professional working relationships with faculty, staff, students and the general public. Sufficient technical ability to master software and systems required to perform job duties at a high level. Ability to accurately organize and maintain records despite frequent interruptions. Ability to exercise sound judgment and discretion in working with confidential information. Job Summary Administrative & Office Support Provides front-line customer service to students, faculty, staff and visitors. Assists with departmental communications and correspondence. Maintains departmental calendars and schedules meetings. Prepares meeting materials and creates agendas and minutes. Maintains organized digital and physical filing systems. Serves as building coordinator; conducts visual facilities checks and coordinate follow-up requests as needed. Human Resources & Personnel Support Assists with hiring paperwork for faculty, staff, adjuncts, tutors and student employees. Coordinates interview scheduling and candidate communications. Supports onboarding for faculty, staff, adjuncts, tutors and student employees. Maintains personnel records and assists with compliance tracking. Student Services, Recruitment & Event Support Assists with student visits and tours. Assists with planning and execution of departmental and college events, including managing registrations, communications and event logistics, coordinating faculty and student participation in recruitment events, and supporting guest speakers, workshops, and departmental and alumni events. Travel & Financial Coordination Assists with travel arrangements and conference logistics for CBT colleagues. Prepares travel authorizations and reimbursement documentation. Tracks deadlines, registrations and expense documentation. Responsible for purchasing and procurement processes related to departmental operations and events. Tutoring & Student Workers Support Maintains tutoring schedules and operational logistics. Tracks student worker hours and assists with payroll coordination. Supports tutoring labs and student success initiatives. Website, Marketing & Communication Support Updates department websites and maintain current information. Assists with newsletters, announcements, email communications and social media. Assists with promotional materials. Supports in-house marketing displays and outreach activities. Data & Records Management Maintains spreadsheets, databases and document repositories. Compiles routine departmental reports and enrollment snapshots. Assists with assessment and accreditation data collection. Travel/Overtime Requirements Telecommuting Employees are not eligible for telecommuting/remote work during their 12-month probationary period. After that time, certain positions may be eligible for telecommuting/remote work at the discretion of the supervisor and in accordance with Winthrop policies. License/Certification Type of Position Classified Position Status Full-Time FLSA Status Non-Exempt Hours Per Week 37.5 Months per Year 9 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2027024S Open Date 08/31/2026 Close Date 09/21/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants PLEASE NOTE * A resume will not be reviewed to determine whether an applicant meets the qualifications outlined in the job vacancy notice (posting). * Responses to supplemental questions are considered part of the application; failure to respond will result in disqualification. NOTICE Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Given the specific duties outlined in the job vacancy notice, list your RELEVANT skills and experience as they relate to administrative support. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience providing support with competing priorities and how you organized work, prioritized tasks and provided communication. (Open Ended Question) * Provide an example of a time you went above and beyond to provide excellent customer service. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/21588": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Spanish",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor of Spanish Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct Instructor of Spanish Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please send the following required materials: 1.    Letter of application and statement of teaching philosophy 2.    Current curriculum vitae 3.    Evidence of teaching excellence (student evaluations, if possible) 4.    Three letters of recommendation 5.    All graduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable for initial review; official transcripts needed for final appointment) The position is available August 1st, 2026 and will be available as enrollment demands require. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact Dr. Scott Shinabargar, Chairs, Department of World Languages and Cultures, at shinabargars@winthrop.edu. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct Instructor of Spanish Job Description The Department of World Languages and Cultures at Winthrop University seeks applications for individuals who can serve as an Adjunct Instructor of Spanish , to teach all levels of Spanish language and culture classes (including dual credit, potentially), and foster students’ interest in continuing language studies. Position Responsibilities About the College To learn more about the College of Arts & Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cas/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/01/2026 Required Qualifications M.A. in Spanish Minimum of 18 credit hours at the graduate level in Spanish Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience at the university level is strongly preferred. Employment Conditions Application Instructions Please send the following required materials: 1.    Letter of application and statement of teaching philosophy 2.    Current curriculum vitae 3.    Evidence of teaching excellence (student evaluations, if possible) 4.    Three letters of recommendation 5.    All graduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable for initial review; official transcripts needed for final appointment) The position is available August 1st, 2026 and will be available as enrollment demands require. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis and continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact Dr. Scott Shinabargar, Chairs, Department of World Languages and Cultures, at shinabargars@winthrop.edu. Open Date 05/13/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2026FC0007P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Faculty-Letter of application and statement of teaching philosophy Curriculum Vitae Faculty-Evidence of teaching excellence Letter of Recommendation Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Faculty-All graduate transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22238": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in Design",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor in Design Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct Instructor in Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Interested individuals are encouraged to submit their credentials as soon as possible for full consideration. Applications should include: A cover letter addressing interest in and qualifications for the position that also includes a statement of teaching philosophy. A current curriculum vitae. Portfolio that includes evidence of teaching excellence (narrative with teaching philosophy) with images of student work and descriptions (URL or PDF). Media file of up to 20 images of the candidate's creative, corporate, and/or scholarly work (URL or PDF). Transcript and evidence of highest degree achieved (unofficial transcripts acceptable at this stage, but official transcripts needed for final appointment). Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct Instructor in Design Job Description Winthrop University, a highly ranked, public, comprehensive university, announces a search for adjunct instructors of design, teaching for the Department of Design within the College of Visual and Performing Arts. Our campus is in Rock Hill, South Carolina, just thirty minutes from Charlotte North Carolina’s thriving design and art market and international airport. This position requires the instructor to teach undergraduate courses, such as Design Fundamentals ( DESF ), Interior Design ( INDS ), or Visual Communication ( VCOM ). Candidates should demonstrate commitment to an interdisciplinary and collaborative approach to design studies, at the foundation, intermediate, and advanced levels. The ideal candidate will demonstrate expertise in design practices including but not limited to game design, graphic design, illustration, and and/or interior design, as well as design research, design thinking, interactive and web design, and interactive digital products. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to high-quality undergraduate teaching, student engagement, and creating a positive learning environment. Position Responsibilities Teach assigned class or classes in the undergraduate design degree, such as studio courses (6 contact hours per week) or lecture (3 contact hours per week), or seminars (from 1-hour to 2.5-hours per week) Prepare course content using a variety of methods Deliver assigned course materials, projects, and examinations consistent with departmental learning outcomes Promote student learning and participation Provide reasonable support to students outside of class meeting times, maintaining office hours on campus, or via video, or other approved means Maintain course records, submit grades by university deadlines, and comply with university academic policies About the College To learn more about the College of Visual & Performing Arts please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cvpa/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2026 Required Qualifications Candidates should hold a terminal degree ( MFA , MDes,) in Design or a related discipline. Candidates holding a bachelor’s degree in design—such as a BA or BFA or BDes, or degree other than an MFA or MDes in design—who have significant teaching and/or professional experience equivalent to a terminal degree, may be considered. Have a demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and work with diverse student populations, and a commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and student engagement Preferred Qualifications Minimum 2–3 years of university-level teaching experience, which could include graduate-level and adjunct teaching. Minimum of 5 years of professional experience in industry. Drawing, drafting, and print production are necessary for our foundations and some upper-level courses. Familiarity with Adobe Creative Cloud, knowledge of printing pre-press principles and printing methodology, and knowledge of user experience design and product design, with an ability to use and demonstrate use of Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign. Interior design instructors should know AutoCad, Revit, SketchUp, codes and standards, and contract documents, as well as rendering techniques with markers. Employment Conditions Position is non-tenure, adjunct position. Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Interested individuals are encouraged to submit their credentials as soon as possible for full consideration. Applications should include: A cover letter addressing interest in and qualifications for the position that also includes a statement of teaching philosophy. A current curriculum vitae. Portfolio that includes evidence of teaching excellence (narrative with teaching philosophy) with images of student work and descriptions ( URL or PDF ). Media file of up to 20 images of the candidate’s creative, corporate, and/or scholarly work ( URL or PDF ). Transcript and evidence of highest degree achieved (unofficial transcripts acceptable at this stage, but official transcripts needed for final appointment). Open Date 07/01/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2026FC0009P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Portfolio Media File Faculty-All graduate transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22303": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct - CAS Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct - CAS Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Please send the following required materials: Cover Letter addressing teaching philosophy and relevant experience. Current Curriculum Vitae (CV). Transcripts (Unofficial documents can support the application. Official transcripts are required for the appointment) Contact information for three professional references. All questions should be directed to casga@winthrop.edu. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct - CAS Job Description The College of Arts and Sciences at Winthrop University seeks dynamic and qualified Adjunct Faculty to teach in disciplines across its 12 academic departments. The ideal candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to high-quality, student-centered instruction that is informed by strong academic credentials and real-world experiences. Applicants should be passionate about fostering student success in an engaging learning environment. Position Responsibilities Adjunct faculty, part-time appointments, are expected to adhere to all policies and procedures expected of university employees. Adjunct faculty will: Offer evidence of effective Student Intellectual Development activities Demonstrate a commitment to meeting the academic responsibility requirements for all faculty (e.g., adherence to academic policies, participating in the collection of assessment data necessary for course and program evaluation). Attend any College orientation sessions. Develop and distribute a written course syllabus as outlined by university policy and College policy at the first course meeting. Present course content as announced to students and as approved by the faculty. Meet all assigned classes or make appropriate alternative arrangements for the class when an absence is unavoidable. Schedule and maintain regular office hours (in-person or virtual) and be available to students. Award academic credit based on the professional evaluation of academic performance. Observe the policies and procedures of the department, College, and the University. Administer student evaluations and any additional assessment instruments required by the University. File an annual report that provides evidence of progress and involvement that is responsive to feedback and meets expectations of rank. About the College To learn more about the College of Arts & Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cas/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2026 Required Qualifications Successful candidates must have a master’s degree and a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the field of instruction. Please specify in the application portal which subject you are qualified to teach given these criteria. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience teaching undergraduate students and proficiency with instructional technology and Learning Management Systems (e.g., Canvas, Blackboard) are preferred. Employment Conditions Position is part-time, adjunct Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Please send the following required materials: Cover Letter addressing teaching philosophy and relevant experience. Current Curriculum Vitae (CV). Transcripts (Unofficial documents can support the application. Official transcripts are required for the appointment) Contact information for three professional references. All questions should be directed to casga@winthrop.edu. Open Date 08/01/2026 Application Review Date 08/01/2026 Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0004P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All graduate transcripts Faculty - List of References Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
