    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22368": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, English",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor, English Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct Instructor, English Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. In your application, please include: Cover letter that addresses the position and includes a statement of teaching philosophy Current curriculum vitae The names and contact information of two people who are willing to act as references for your application All graduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable for initial review; official transcripts needed for final appointment) For more information, contact Dr. Leslie Bickford, Director of Composition, Department of English, bickfordl@winthrop.edu at (803) 323-4564. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct Instructor, English Job Description The Department of English at Winthrop University is seeking applications for part-time adjunct instructor position with the expertise needed to serve as an Adjunct Instructor of English. The ideal candidate will be a dedicated and experienced individual who can teach introductory courses in Composition and Rhetoric, specifically Writing 101, Introduction to Academic Discourse. The Winthrop Department of English boasts a vibrant team of faculty known for their engaging teaching in classes that serve students from diverse backgrounds and learning communities. The department also collaborates with other departments on campus to deliver its major curriculum for double/dual majors, as well as secondary education degrees. Position Responsibilities Teaching one or more sections of Writing 101, Introduction to Academic Discourse. Possibly training for and teaching the second and/or third courses in Winthrop’s General Education core, The Human Experience ( HMXP 102) and Critical Reading, Thinking, and Writing ( CRTW 201) during the spring semester. WRIT 101 sections are not guaranteed in the spring semester. Fostering students’ interest in academic writing and critical thinking. Coordinating the department’s delivery of the Gen Ed core (reviewing/choosing materials, establishing common syllabi, etc.). Engaging in departmental support and academic responsibility, including holding two office hours per week per section taught. About the College To learn more about the College of Arts & Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cas/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2026 Required Qualifications Master’s in English or Creative Writing, with at least 18 hrs. of coursework in English and Writing courses completed at the graduate level. Preferred Qualifications Employment Conditions part-time, adjunct instructor Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. In your application, please include: Cover letter that addresses the position and includes a statement of teaching philosophy Current curriculum vitae The names and contact information of two people who are willing to act as references for your application All graduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable for initial review; official transcripts needed for final appointment) For more information, contact Dr. Leslie Bickford, Director of Composition, Department of English, bickfordl@winthrop.edu at (803) 323-4564. Open Date 08/03/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0006P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All graduate transcripts Faculty - List of References Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22486": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Double Bass Instructor",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct, Double Bass Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct, Double Bass Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin on Auguist 12, 2026 and continues until the position is filled. For more information, please email Lorrie Crochet at crochetl@winthrop.edu. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct, Double Bass Instructor Job Description Instructor for applied double bass lessons as assigned. Position Responsibilities Teach applied double bass lessons as assigned. About the College To learn more about the College of Visual & Performing Arts please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cvpa/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/24/2026 Required Qualifications Master of Music in Double Bass Performance (or equivalent) Experience teaching private double bass lessons Preferred Qualifications Employment Conditions Position is non-tenure track, adjunct Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin on Auguist 12, 2026 and continues until the position is filled. For more information, please email Lorrie Crochet at crochetl@winthrop.edu. Open Date 08/12/2026 Application Review Date 08/12/2026 Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0008P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Faculty-All graduate transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22593": {
      "title": "Part-Time Instructor of History",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Part-Time Instructor of History Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Part-Time Instructor of History Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Letter of application that addresses the position, with statement of teaching philosophy Current curriculum vita Evidence of teaching excellence Names and contact information for 2 references All graduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable for initial review; official transcripts needed for final appointment) For more information, contact: Dr. Gregory Bell Professor of History and Chair bellgd@winthrop.edu 803-323-4674 Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Part-Time Instructor of History Job Description The Department of History at Winthrop University is seeking applications for part-time adjunct instructor position with the expertise needed to serve as an Instructor of History. The ideal candidate will be a dedicated and experienced individual who can teach introductory courses on World Civilizations, specifically HIST 111 (World Civilizations from Antiquity to 950 CE), HIST 112 (World Civilizations from 950 – 1750 CE), or HIST 113 (World Civilizations from 1750 – present). The Winthrop Department of History boasts an exceptional team of faculty known for their engaging teaching in classes that serve students from diverse backgrounds and learning communities. The department also collaborates with other departments on campus to deliver its major curriculum for double/dual majors, as well as secondary education degrees. Position Responsibilities Teaching one or more sections of HIST 111 (World Civilizations from Antiquity to 950 CE), HIST 112 (World Civilizations from 950 – 1750 CE), or HIST 113 (World Civilizations from 1750 – present). Possibly training for and teaching an upper-level history course in the area of expertise of the candidate. Fostering students’ interest in academic writing and critical thinking. Coordinating the department’s delivery of the Gen Ed core (reviewing/choosing materials, establishing common syllabi, etc.). Engaging in departmental support and academic responsibility, including holding two office hours per week per section taught. About the College To learn more about the College of Arts & Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cas/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2026 Required Qualifications M.A. in History, with at least 18 hrs. of coursework in History courses completed at the graduate level. Preferred Qualifications Candidate has a background in European History and can teach courses on that topic. Employment Conditions Position is non-tenure-track, adjunct Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Letter of application that addresses the position, with statement of teaching philosophy Current curriculum vita Evidence of teaching excellence Names and contact information for 2 references All graduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable for initial review; official transcripts needed for final appointment) For more information, contact: Dr. Gregory Bell Professor of History and Chair bellgd@winthrop.edu 803-323-4674 Open Date Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0003P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-Evidence of teaching excellence Faculty - List of References Faculty-All graduate transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22622": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct - Online Marketing for Arts Administration and Capstone Advisor (MAAA) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct - Online Marketing for Arts Administration and Capstone Advisor (MAAA) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin on August 26, 2026 and continues until positions are filled. For more information, please contact scanlank@winthrop.edu. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct - Online Marketing for Arts Administration and Capstone Advisor (MAAA) Job Description Winthrop University’s College of Visual and Performing Arts ( CVPA ) seeks qualified adjunct faculty with expertise in marketing for arts and cultural organizations to teach graduate-level courses in the Master of Arts in Arts Administration ( MAAA ) program and to be part of a pool of Capstone Advisors. Courses are delivered in a 100% online format and typically serve working professionals and emerging arts leaders. Position Responsibilities Teaching assigned graduate course(s) online, using the University’s LMS , Blackboard Designing and facilitating high-quality online learning experiences (weekly modules, discussions, feedback, assessments, video lectures) Providing timely communication, grading, and student support Aligning course outcomes, activities, and assessments with program expectations Collaborating with the Program Director on course planning, consistency, and continuous improvement Maintaining appropriate academic documentation (syllabus, grade records, assessment artifacts) About the College To learn more about the College of Visual & Performing Arts please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cvpa/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Not applicable Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 01/01/2026 Required Qualifications Adjunct faculty teaching graduate courses at Winthrop University must have a master’s degree or higher in the teaching discipline or a related discipline. A terminal degree ( MFA or doctorate) is preferred as well as professional experience in the subject being taught. Preferred Qualifications Employment Conditions Adjunct, part-time Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin on August 26, 2026 and continues until positions are filled. For more information, please contact scanlank@winthrop.edu. Open Date 08/26/2026 Application Review Date 08/26/2026 Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0009P PositionType: Adjunct Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All graduate transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22691": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Police Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Police Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Police Officer State Title Law Enforcement Officer I State Class Code JC10 State Pay Table LAW Annual Salary/Hiring Range $50,000 for applicants not certified as South Carolina Law Enforcement Officer (LEO). Salary for certified S.C. LEOs based on years of certification. Job Purpose Reporting to the Police Sergeant, the Campus Police Officer protects students, faculty, staff and visitors, property, and facilities and enforces the laws and regulations of the City of Rock Hill, State of South Carolina and Winthrop University on University, adjacent and other appropriate properties. Required Qualifications High school diploma; certification as a Law Enforcement Officer by the South Carolina Justice Academy or willingness to obtain and maintain; certification as a NCIC Full Function Operator by the South Carolina Law Enforcement Division or willingness to obtain and maintain; and a valid driver’s license required. Must reside in South Carolina or be willing to relocate to South Carolina. Must be at least 21 years of age. Preferred Qualifications Previous related law enforcement experience highly desired. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Summary Working knowledge of the Rock Hill City Code, the laws of the state of South Carolina, and the rules and regulations of Winthrop University pertaining to campus security, including civil rights laws. Ability to investigate accidents, disturbances and violations; and deal tactfully and effectively with students, faculty, staff and the general public. Effective interpersonal and communication skills. Must be able to work rotating shifts, including nights, weekends and holidays. Must pass the state physical examination, qualify semi-annually with firearm, and successfully complete defensive driving requirements. Job Summary Patrols in WUPD vehicles or on foot to enforce City of Rock Hill and State of South Carolina laws and regulations and Winthrop University policies. Issues citations for moving and parking violations. Investigates complaints and disturbances using the appropriate techniques and makes arrests as necessary. Prepares various reports and forms, including incident, citation, accident and information reports, case files, tow sheets, and field interview cards. Performs building security inspections. Responds to requests for assistance. Monitors parking areas and crosswalks and reports maintenance needs. Controls traffic during fire drills and emergencies. Travel/Overtime Requirements Telecommuting Employees are not eligible for telecommuting/remote work during their 12-month probationary period. After that time, certain positions may be eligible for telecommuting/remote work at the discretion of the supervisor and in accordance with Winthrop policies. License/Certification Type of Position Classified Position Status Full-Time FLSA Status Non-Exempt Hours Per Week 40 Months per Year 12 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2027015S Open Date 07/30/2026 Close Date 09/14/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants PLEASE NOTE * A resume will not be reviewed to determine whether an applicant meets the qualifications outlined in the job vacancy notice (posting). * Responses to supplemental questions are considered part of the application; failure to respond will result in disqualification. NOTICE Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you willing to participate in the pre-employment physical fitness test? Yes No * Do you understand that the annual salary listed in the posting is not negotiable? Yes No * Are you at least 21 years old? Yes No * Are you currently or have you ever been a Certified Class 1 Law Enforcement Officer (Police Officer or Sheriff's Deputy) in South Carolina? Currently certified Previously certified No * If you answered \"Yes\" to question No. 4, provide the date you graduated from the South Carolina Criminal Justice Academy. If you answered \"No,\" indicate N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked for a law enforcement agency outside the state of South Carolina? Yes No * If you answered Yes to question No. 6, list the agency(ies), date(s) and certification. If you answered No, indicate N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Are you able to perform the essential job functions as outlined in the vacancy notice with or without a reasonable accommodation? Yes No * Are you able to wear a respirator and other personal protective equipment without restrictions for emergencies and training exercises? Yes No * Do you reside in South Carolina and, if not, are you willing to relocate? Yes No * Are you willing and able to work rotating shifts, including nights, weekends and holidays? Yes No * Provide your driver’s license number and the state in which it was issued. (By providing this information, you consent to a preliminary criminal background check through the South Carolina Law Enforcement Division and a driving record check. Failure to provide this information may exclude you from consideration for this position.) (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22781": {
      "title": "Finance Associate",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Finance Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Finance Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Finance Associate State Title Fiscal Technician II State Class Code AD03 State Pay Table GEN Annual Salary/Hiring Range $42,085 Job Purpose Reporting to the Business Center Manager, the Finance Associate processes financial transactions related to travel, procurement, accounts payable and receivable, accounting and asset management for the Center’s assigned departments, ensuring accuracy and compliance with all applicable institutional, state and federal regulations, policies and procedures. Required Qualifications High school diploma and four years of finance experience; an equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Intermediate proficiency with Microsoft Excel. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Adobe and Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, and SharePoint. Experience working as part of a service team. Experience with Banner or similar integrated software system. Relevant experience at an institution of higher education. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Summary Knowledge of finance and payroll terminology and practices. Knowledge of federal and state laws and guidelines related to business practices preferred. Effective oral and written communication skills. Exceptional organizational skills. Effective interpersonal skills and the ability to establish and maintain positive relationships within and outside of reporting lines. Willingness and demonstrated ability to learn new hardware and software systems. Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality in compliance with rules and regulations, including HIPAA and FERPA . Proven ability and dedication to meeting deadlines. Demonstrated ability to work with accuracy and attention to detail in a high-volume environment. Job Summary Procurement Determines and executes the appropriate procurement procedures for routine purchases, including referrals to Information Technology for technology procurement, institutional software contracts and purchase order support. Ensures a complete W-9 is on file for all vendors, vendor profiles in Banner are complete and accurate, and vendors have been reviewed for independent contractor/employment classification. Ensures independent contractors have a current contract. Reviews requisitions for potential fixed-asset implications and notifies the appropriate functional offices. Reviews and reconciles purchasing card (P-Card) transactions for appropriate funding, policy compliance and completion. Maintains financial records and files. Assists in preparing routine, standardized reports. Responds to department questions regarding P-Card use and escalates complex procurement processing concerns. Travel Assists employees and students in submitting travel authorization requests, including recording commitments in Banner. Reviews and processes routine employee, student and group travel authorization requests. Reviews and processes requests for and reconciliation of travel-related cash advances and out-of-pocket expenses, including those processed on a P-Card. Retains financial records and files according to adopted naming conventions, organization and record retention protocols. Assists in preparing routine, standardized reports. Fields employee questions and escalates complex travel processing concerns. Accounts Payable Reviews and routes invoices from third-party vendors and completes or routes change order requests. Reviews routine check requests to ensure they are complete and comply with policy. Reviews requests to pay independent contractors and determines whether they meet IRS regulations. Retains financial records and files according to adopted naming conventions, organization and record retention protocols. Assists in preparing routine, standardized reports. Fields employee questions and escalates complex concerns to the appropriate person. Budget Addresses or routes budget-related inquiries. Addresses or routes user questions related to Banner Finance and related modules. Reviews initial budget submissions for compliance with guidelines and mathematical accuracy. Retains financial records and files according to adopted naming conventions, organization and record retention protocols. Assists in preparing routine, standardized reports. Accounting Assists in preparing routine, standardized reports. Fields employee questions and escalates complex concerns to the appropriate person. Other Duties Creates and maintains procedural documentation. Performs other related duties as required, including serving as backup for other members of the assigned Business Center. Travel/Overtime Requirements Occasional work outside normal business hours. Telecommuting Employees are not eligible for telecommuting/remote work during their 12-month probationary period. After that time, certain positions may be eligible for telecommuting/remote work at the discretion of the supervisor and in accordance with Winthrop policies. License/Certification Type of Position Classified Position Status Full-Time FLSA Status Non-Exempt Hours Per Week 37.5 Months per Year 12 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2027025S Open Date 09/02/2026 Close Date 09/13/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants PLEASE NOTE * A resume will not be reviewed to determine whether an applicant meets the qualifications outlined in the job vacancy notice (posting). * Responses to supplemental questions are considered part of the application; failure to respond will result in disqualification. NOTICE Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have intermediate proficiency in Microsoft Excel? Yes No * Describe in detail your skills in Microsoft Excel. Include your familiarity with pivot tables, aggregation formulas, lookup functions, and any formulas or functions with which you have intermediate proficiency. (Open Ended Question) * Provide an example that shows your ability to be successful in a fast-paced environment and/or juggle multiple competing priorities. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your customer service experience and provide an example of a time you went above and beyond your normal job duties to provide exceptional customer service. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/21982": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Management",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor of Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct Instructor of Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. For more information, please contact Dr. Joanna R. Jackson at jacksonjr@winthrop.edu ; 803-323-2961. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct Instructor of Management Job Description The Department of Management and Marketing at Winthrop University invites applications for an adjunct instructor to teach undergraduate management courses, with primary responsibility for MGMT 331: Unicorns and Dragons. This course emphasizes inclusive leadership, organizational behavior, workplace culture, communication, and the development of career-ready professionals through active learning and applied experiences. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to high quality undergraduate teaching, student engagement, and creating an positive learning environment. Depending on departmental needs and qualifications, the adjunct may also teach additional undergraduate management courses. Position Responsibilities Teach assigned undergraduate management courses, primarily MGMT 331 Prepare and deliver engaging instruction using a variety of teaching methods that promote student learning and participation Maintain regular communication with students and provide timely feedback on assignments and assessments Develop and administer course materials, assignments, and examinations consistent with departmental learning outcomes Maintain accurate course records, submit grades by university deadlines, and comply with university academic policies Hold reasonable availability for student consultation through office hours or other approved means About the College To learn more about the College of Business & Technology please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cbt/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2026 Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Management, Human Resource Management, Organizational Leadership, Business Administration, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. Relevant professional experience in management, leadership, human resources, organizational development, diversity and inclusion, consulting, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and work with diverse student populations.  Commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and student engagement. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate (Ph.D., D.B.A., Ed.D., or other relevant terminal degree) in Management, Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Leadership, Business Administration, or a closely related field. Prior college or university teaching experience, particularly in undergraduate management courses. Experience teaching or facilitating topics related to leadership, organizational behavior, workplace culture, diversity and inclusion, teamwork, conflict management, or professional development. Experience incorporating experiential learning, case studies, simulations, project-based learning, or community engagement into instruction. Employment Conditions Position is non-tenure, adjunct position. Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. For more information, please contact Dr. Joanna R. Jackson at jacksonjr@winthrop.edu ; 803-323-2961. Open Date 06/29/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2026FC0008P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All graduate transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22240": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Instructor of Dance",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct - Instructor of Dance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct - Instructor of Dance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Please send the following required materials: Cover Letter Current Curriculum Vitae (CV). Transcripts (Unofficial documents can support the application. Official transcripts are required for the appointment) Contact information for three professional references. For more information, please contact: Daniel Gordon Chair and Professor Department of Theatre & Dance gordond@winthrop.edu and/or Kelly Ozust Associate Professor of Dance and Dance Program Director ozustk@winthrop.edu Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct - Instructor of Dance Job Description Teach contemporary and/or jazz and/or ballet technique at all levels. Position Responsibilities Teach contemporary and/or jazz and/or ballet technique at all levels. Opportunity to choreograph for departmental musical theatre of dance productions. Teach other technique courses and dance theory courses based on expertise/interest. About the College To learn more about the College of Visual & Performing Arts please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cvpa/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2026 Required Qualifications Expertise and interest to teach contemporary and/or jazz and/or ballet technique at all levels Experience choreographing dance or musical theatre productions at the college level Evidence of effective interpersonal skills Evidence of proven success working in a team-oriented environment Adjunct faculty teaching undergraduate courses at Winthrop University are expected to possess at least 18 hours of graduate credits in the discipline. In cases of exceptional and significant professional experiences, the said experience may be considered in lieu of these credits Preferred Qualifications B.A. or M.F.A. in dance Employment Conditions Position is part-time, adjunct Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Please send the following required materials: Cover Letter Current Curriculum Vitae (CV). Transcripts (Unofficial documents can support the application. Official transcripts are required for the appointment) Contact information for three professional references. For more information, please contact: Daniel Gordon Chair and Professor Department of Theatre & Dance gordond@winthrop.edu and/or Kelly Ozust Associate Professor of Dance and Dance Program Director ozustk@winthrop.edu Open Date 07/21/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0005P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All graduate transcripts Faculty - List of References Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22337": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Sociology",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Sociology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant Professor in Sociology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. First consideration will be given to applications received on or before August 15, 2026. Applications received after the deadline may be considered if a suitable candidate has not been found. Letter of application that addresses the position, with statement of teaching philosophy Cover letter that includes ways the candidate can contribute to Winthrop's curriculum and a planned research trajectory; A curriculum vitae; Graduate transcripts demonstrating a terminal degree or a master's degree with at least 18hrs in the discipline (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for the initial review; official transcripts must be provided for a final appointment) Letters of recommendation from three academic professionals List with contact information for three professional references Please address questions to Dr. Brad Tripp, Department Chair (trippb@winthrop.edu). Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Assistant Professor in Sociology Job Description The Winthrop University Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Anthropology invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track position beginning January 1, 2027. The successful candidate will have an active research agenda and be able to teach a variety of courses in a combined sociology program, particularly courses within the General Sociology and Social Inequalities Concentrations. Candidates will also teach Social Theory and Qualitative Research Methods. The area of specialization should allow the individual to contribute coursework in at least one of the following areas: Sociology of Technology, the User Experience (UX) research Concentration, Medical Sociology, and/or Urban Sociology. The preferred candidate will demonstrate potential for teaching and research involving students from diverse ethnic, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds. Requirements for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor include a Ph.D. in sociology or related field ( ABD will be considered), evidence of teaching excellence and commitment to student learning, and evidence of an ongoing program of research and publication. We seek a broadly trained teacher-scholar interested in involving undergraduate students in experiential learning. The candidate will also advise undergraduates and participate in other service to the university. The department supports a thriving B.A. program in sociology with concentrations in anthropology, social inequalities, criminology, pre-law, and User Experience (UX) Research, as well as a separate B.A. in Criminal Justice. Winthrop, a small public comprehensive university, boasts a highly diverse student body of approximately 5,000 students and has been a top-ranked regional university for more than 20 consecutive years. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach undergraduate Sociology courses, including introductory Sociology, Social Inequalities, and Social Theory/Qualitative Research Methods Develop and deliver engaging instruction using various teaching modalities Maintain a standard teaching load of 12 contact hours per semester. Provide academic advising and mentorship to undergraduate students. Develop and sustain a scholarly identity and an independent research program that will spark student interests in programs housed in the Sociology, Criminology, and Anthropology department. Participate actively in university service, including committee work, curriculum development and campus initiatives. Contribute to a supportive and inclusive learning environment that promotes student achievement and academic excellence Have strong interpersonal skills and an overall commitment to student success and engagement About the College To learn more about the College of Arts & Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cas/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits At Winthrop University, we are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package that significantly enhances the total compensation for our employees. In partnership with the State of South Carolina and the Public Employee Benefit Authority ( PEBA ), our benefits include health and life insurance, generous paid leave, parental leave, and retirement programs. These benefits reflect our commitment to supporting the well-being and financial security of our employees. For more information please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/hr/employee-benefits.aspx Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 01/01/2026 Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Sociology or related field is required for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor ( ABD will be considered) Experience teaching or demonstrated potential to teach sociology courses including Social Theory and Qualitative Research methods. Evidence of teaching excellence and an ongoing commitment to student learning Evidence of ongoing program of research, ideally involving undergraduates, and the potential for publication Strong oral and written communication skills Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability to contribute to one or more of the following areas: Sociology of Technology, the User Experience (UX) Research Concentration, Medical Sociology, and/or Urban Sociology Experience mentoring undergraduate research including, but not limited to, research lab supervision, coauthoring with students, and bringing students to conferences Interest in contributing to the major by offering a wide variety of courses including introductory courses Research that compliments existing departmental expertise and highlights the applied nature of sociology. Employment Conditions Position is full-time, nine-month, tenure-track with an expectation of summer employment. Salary is commensurate with qualifications. Application Instructions First consideration will be given to applications received on or before August 15, 2026. Applications received after the deadline may be considered if a suitable candidate has not been found. Letter of application that addresses the position, with statement of teaching philosophy Cover letter that includes ways the candidate can contribute to Winthrop’s curriculum and a planned research trajectory; A curriculum vitae; Graduate transcripts demonstrating a terminal degree or a master’s degree with at least 18hrs in the discipline (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for the initial review; official transcripts must be provided for a final appointment) Letters of recommendation from three academic professionals List with contact information for three professional references Please address questions to Dr. Brad Tripp, Department Chair (trippb@winthrop.edu). Open Date 07/02/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0002P PositionType: Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Faculty-Letter of application and statement of teaching philosophy Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All graduate transcripts Letter of Recommendation Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Faculty - List of References Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22437": {
      "title": "Career Coach",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Career Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Career Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Career Coach State Title Student Svcs Prog Coord II State Class Code CB70 State Pay Table GEN Annual Salary/Hiring Range $50,198 Job Purpose Reporting to the Director of the Center for Career Development and Internships, the Career Coach assists students with all phases of the career development process. Required Qualifications Master’s degree, preferably in Counseling, Higher Education, Student Affairs, Business, Human Resources, Organizational Development/Communication or related. Preferred Qualifications Two years of experience in student counseling, career coaching, career services, higher education or placement services. Experience in public relations and/or communications. Training, experience, and certification career assessments (e.g., Myers-Briggs Type Indicator ( MBTI ), Strong Interest Inventory) and computer-guided career assessments. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Summary Working knowledge of career assessments and counseling/coaching techniques. Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. Exceptional interpersonal skills and the ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships that build rapport with all constituents (students, alumni, faculty, staff, employers, parents and families). Ability to use community knowledge and research and networking skills to grow experiential opportunities. Demonstrated ability to teach, train, facilitate and make presentations. Ability to use technology, including social media, to increase efficiencies/enhance effectiveness. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, including Excel, Word, Outlook and PowerPoint, and Handshake or similar career services management system. Demonstrated commitment and ability to work successfully with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Demonstrated ability to utilize AI ethically and effectively, and to coach students on the same skills. Job Summary Career Coaching Provides a regular schedule of individual career coaching appointments and drop-ins for students and alumni. May at times provide group career coaching sessions. Evaluates student needs and provides appropriate resources and support, which might include career assessments and interpretation, resume assistance, job/internship search and interview preparation, and/or assistance developing a career plan. Guides students through career assessments and offers understanding and resources to help them research and develop individualized solutions as they make life-changing decisions. Utilizes online career management systems (e.g., Handshake, Big Interview), to support student career development and helps students navigate complex challenges in their career development efforts. Documents appropriate notes and records to track students’ engagement and progress. Promotes Winthrop’s Alumni Mentoring Program through coaching interactions. Career Readiness Presentations and Workshops Conducts career presentations and workshops in the classroom by faculty invitation, at campus conferences and events, and to student organizations. Develops, coordinates, and facilitates training and skill development workshops, to include resume preparation, job/internship search strategies, interviewing, experiential learning preparation, networking, LinkedIn, and professionalism. Collaborates with other CDI colleagues on customizing and tailoring content, activities, and materials for different student audiences and desired learning outcomes. Co-plan and co-present certain programs when appropriate, with CDI colleagues as well as other campus colleagues. Utilizes a variety of delivery methods: workshops, lectures, presentations, meetings, and e-learning. Represents the CDI at other Winthrop events, such as Admissions events, Study Abroad Fair, Orientation, etc. typically via tabling but can include presentations to students, families, and guests. Marketing & Communications Oversees and manages social media channels for the career center. Creates processes and calendars to organize social posts and campaigns. Hires, trains, and supervises Marketing Coordinator (student employee) to develop promotional and outreach campaigns to attract student awareness of resources and services, as well as participation in events, career fairs, and programs. Collaborates with career center colleagues to source information, resources, and people to feature in social communications. Support the Center’s Employer Engagement strategies by promoting the use of Handshake for internships and part- and full-time job postings. Career Events Contributes to the team activities during the coordination of on-campus career fairs and related events, including networking events, industry meetups, etiquette dinners and receptions, and so forth. Activities include set up and breakdown activities, greeting employers, managing student and alumni check-in stations, collecting student and employer surveys, and assists where needed when other CDI team members are unavailable. Supports the Associate Director and Director with the implementation of tailored career and competency-building events, such as resume and mock interview days, career panels, and networking after-hours. Communicates with campus departments, employers, alumni, and students and works with the career center team to increase student awareness and engagement in events. Interview Preparation Software Management Manages the administration of mock interview software (e.g., Big Interview), including compiling analytics and reports and communicating periodically with the company representative for updates, support, and ongoing learning opportunities. Prepares teaching and training materials for all users (e.g., tips for students on how to access the platform, information for faculty on creating a class assignment). Manages the coordination of class and group assignments within the platform and liaises with faculty and staff. Designs promotional materials to encourage student utilization of the platform (e.g., flyers, videos, social media posts). Travel/Overtime Requirements Ability to travel and work flexible hours as needed. Telecommuting Employees are not eligible for telecommuting/remote work during their 12-month probationary period. After that time, certain positions may be eligible for telecommuting/remote work at the discretion of the supervisor and in accordance with Winthrop policies. License/Certification Certification in Myers-Briggs (MBTI) and/or Strong Interest Inventory preferred. Type of Position Classified Position Status Full-Time FLSA Status Exempt Hours Per Week 37.5 Months per Year 12 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2027020S Open Date 08/07/2026 Close Date 09/13/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants PLEASE NOTE * A resume will not be reviewed to determine whether an applicant meets the qualifications outlined in the job vacancy notice (posting). * Responses to supplemental questions are considered part of the application; failure to respond will result in disqualification. NOTICE Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your career coaching/advising experience. (Open Ended Question) * Describe in detail the extent of your experience with career and personality assessments, such as Myers Briggs (MBTI) and Strong Interest Inventory (SII). (Open Ended Question) * Provide an example of a strategy you used (or would use) to increase student engagement with career center resources, services, programs and events. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience with career management systems, mock interview programs and similar technology. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
