    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22873": {
      "title": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Budget Analyst Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Budget Analyst Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Budget Analyst State Title Accountant/Fiscal Analyst II State Class Code AD22 State Pay Table GEN Annual Salary/Hiring Range $62,805 Job Purpose Reporting to the Budget Manager, the Budget Analyst is responsible for position budgeting and operational budget entry. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in accounting or similar with at least 15 semester hours in accounting-related courses and at least two years of relevant institution-level business, finance, payroll and/or budget experience. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Intermediate proficiency with Microsoft Excel. Preferred Qualifications Accounting experience at an institution of higher education. Experience with Ellucian Banner Finance Software. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Summary Working knowledge of the principles and theories of budgeting and financial management. Knowledge of basic accounting principles and practices. Exceptional organizational, customer service, and oral and written communication skills. Effective interpersonal skills and the ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students and the general public. Sufficient technical skills to master software required to perform job duties. Ability to handle confidential information discretely. Ability to perform data entry with speed and accuracy. Strong analytical and research skills. Ability to exercise sound professional judgment and work with attention to detail and accuracy. Job Summary Position Control Management Reviews hiring proposals and salary actions and verifies funding in Banner Finance. Works closely with Human Resources and the Payroll Office to resolve payroll issues. Manages positions for all assignments: Ensures labor distribution coding is accurate; identifies and calculates corrections to labor distribution and loads them in Banner; and establishes and funds new positions as needed. Processes encumbrance liquidations. Maintains personnel roster and vacancy reports. Budget Entry Loads budgets. Completes budget transfers. Calculates and enters course fee, lab fee and carryforward budgets. Budget Research & Documentation Completes ad hoc budget research. Supports the resolution of overspent budgets. Performs routine and ad hoc budget analysis. Creates and maintains procedural documentation. Other Collaborates with continuous improvement projects. Supports employees with budget functions in Banner. Sends communication and Daily Digests with budget updates and information. Travel/Overtime Requirements Telecommuting Employees are not eligible for telecommuting/remote work during their 12-month probationary period. After that time, certain positions may be eligible for telecommuting/remote work at the discretion of the supervisor and in accordance with Winthrop policies. License/Certification Type of Position Classified Position Status Full-Time FLSA Status Exempt Hours Per Week 37.5 Months per Year 12 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2027028S Open Date 09/15/2026 Close Date 09/21/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants PLEASE NOTE * A resume will not be reviewed to determine whether an applicant meets the qualifications outlined in the job vacancy notice (posting). * Responses to supplemental questions are considered part of the application; failure to respond will result in disqualification. NOTICE Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Given the duties and requirements outlined in the job vacancy notice, list in bullet format your relevant skills and experience. (Open Ended Question) * Rate your proficiency with Excel and indicate how you have used spreadsheets in your current or previous position. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22880": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Biology (Neuroscience)",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Biology (Neuroscience) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant Professor, Biology (Neuroscience) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The application review process begins October 23, 2026. Materials received after this date may be considered if an acceptable candidate has not been found. Applicants must submit the following materials electronically: Letter of application Curriculum vitae (CV) including the names, phone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references from whom recommendation letters can be requested. Detailed statement of teaching philosophy. Detailed statement of future research plans. Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment). Student course evaluations and/or other evidence of excellence in teaching. Three letters of recommendation will be requested from semifinalists at a later date. (The CV must include the names, phone numbers, and email addresses for all references.) For questions about the position, please contact: Chair of the Search Committee – Neuroscience Kristi M. Westover Department of Biology Winthrop University Rock Hill, SC 29733 Phone: 803-323-1227 Fax: 803-323-3448 Email: westoverk@winthrop.edu Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Assistant Professor, Biology (Neuroscience) Job Description Winthrop University invites applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Biology with expertise in neuroscience for employment to begin August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will join a collegial environment that includes 14 full-time faculty and over 300 undergraduate majors. The successful candidate will demonstrate evidence of excellence in teaching, a strong commitment to student learning and development, and the ability to establish an independent research program that attracts undergraduate students. This position requires a Ph.D. in a biological science or an equivalent area (ABDs will be considered). Review of applications will begin on October 23, 2026. Application materials received after this date may be considered if an acceptable candidate has not been found. Position Responsibilities Teach/develop courses in neuroscience and support the biology curriculum for a total of 12 contact hours per semester. Beyond neuroscience, teach courses that could include Principles of Cell and Molecular Biology, Scientific Process in Biology, Anatomy and Physiology, Integration of Biological Principles, and courses that contribute to the general education program. Active engagement in student-centered research in field of specialization. Advising and mentoring undergraduate students majoring in biology. Engage in professional service to the department, college, university, discipline, and community Other duties as assigned by the department chair. About the College To learn more about the College of Arts & Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cas/ . About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,200-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits At Winthrop University, we are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package that significantly enhances the total compensation for our employees. In partnership with the State of South Carolina and the Public Employee Benefit Authority ( PEBA ), our benefits include health and life insurance, generous paid leave, parental leave, and retirement programs. These benefits reflect our commitment to supporting the well-being and financial security of our employees. For more information please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/hr/employee-benefits.aspx . Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2027 Required Qualifications Ph.D. in a biological science with a strong background in neuroscience. ABDs will be considered for appointment at the rank of instructor if all degree requirements are not completed by the expected start date of August 16, 2027. Ability to teach neuroscience and additional courses including Principles of Cell and Molecular Biology, Scientific Process in Biology, Anatomy and Physiology, Integration of Biological Principles, and courses that contribute to the general education program. Microscopy expertise is desirable. Evidence of an ability to establish an independent research program that will include undergraduate students. Evidence of excellent interpersonal skills and strong personal ethics for mentorship of student research projects. Preferred Qualifications In addition to the qualifications above, those with expertise in microscopy will be given preference. Employment Conditions This is a full-time, tenure-track appointment requiring daily on-campus contact; instructional duties during the academic year (9 months, Aug. 16 – May 15) come with the option to actively support a summer undergraduate research experience. Application Instructions The application review process begins October 23, 2026. Materials received after this date may be considered if an acceptable candidate has not been found. Applicants must submit the following materials electronically: Letter of application Curriculum vitae (CV) including the names, phone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references from whom recommendation letters can be requested. Detailed statement of teaching philosophy. Detailed statement of future research plans. Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment). Student course evaluations and/or other evidence of excellence in teaching. Three letters of recommendation will be requested from semifinalists at a later date. (The CV must include the names, phone numbers, and email addresses for all references.) For questions about the position, please contact: Chair of the Search Committee – Neuroscience Kristi M. Westover Department of Biology Winthrop University Rock Hill, SC 29733 Phone: 803-323-1227 Fax: 803-323-3448 Email: westoverk@winthrop.edu Open Date 09/15/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0019P PositionType: Faculty Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Faculty - Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Faculty - Statement of Teaching Philosophy Faculty - Statement of Research Interests Faculty-All transcripts Faculty-Evidence of teaching excellence Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22886": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Fiscal Services/Controller",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Associate Vice President for Fiscal Services/Controller Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Associate Vice President for Fiscal Services/Controller Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Associate Vice President for Fiscal Services/Controller State Title Associate Vice President State Class Code UC61 State Pay Table Annual Salary/Hiring Range $144,458; actual salary depends on qualifications. Job Purpose Reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Business Affairs, the Associate Vice President/Controller ( AVP /C) provides fiscal leadership and strategic oversight of financial accounting, university business and budgeting processes, and control compliance. Designs and implements systems and processes based on best practices to support the university’s mission and strategic plan; Ensures compliance with local, state, and federal regulations and the timely submission of internal and external reports; Fosters a commitment to continuous improvement and outstanding service and works to strengthen collaboration across campus and with external constituencies; and Provides supervisory leadership to accounting services, accounts payable, budget services, payroll services, post-award management and student financial services. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in accounting or finance. Seven years of experience in finance, accounting, budget management or related field. At least three years of supervisory experience. Preferred Qualifications Certified Public Accountant ( CPA ) credential. At least five years of experience directing or managing fund accounting and working with GASB accounting and financial reporting standards and FASB reporting, preferably at an institution of higher education. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Summary Expert knowledge of generally accepted accounting principles ( GAAP ) and government accounting standards and regulations. Working knowledge of the taxes normally associated with a public institution of higher education. Ability to interpret and apply complex guidelines, rules, and regulations. Strong financial skills and proven ability to plan and manage operating and capital budgets and support a data-driven decision model. Exceptional problem-solving skills and the ability to think strategically and develop a vision for long-range planning. Proven leader and manager who knows how to motivate a team, support their professional development and create a productive work environment. Exceptional communication skills and the ability to make effective oral and written presentations at the executive level. Must be detail-oriented, possess exceptional time-management and organizational skills, and be committed to delivering work on assigned schedules. Strong commitment to transparency, follow through, and customer service and the ability to monitor and evaluate service quality. Familiarity with higher education operations and proficiency with ERP systems common to higher education. Effective interpersonal skills and the demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with individuals at all levels of an organization. Job Summary Financial Operations Leadership and Compliance Plans, directs and administers the university’s financial operations, including accounting, post award management, accounts payable, payroll, fixed-asset accounting, resource planning and allocation, budget management, purchasing, P-Card administration, risk management, cash management, cashiering, student billing and accounts receivable. Builds and maintains effective, high-functioning, cross-relational teams within the fiscal operations units. Anticipates and leads change with understanding; considers various perspectives and uses appropriate tools to make informed changes and implement them effectively and efficiently. Establishes and maintains policies, procedures, systems and internal controls that are based on best practices, support the university’s strategic plan and ensure compliance with state and federal laws. Anticipates changes in laws, rules, regulations and standards affecting higher education and ensures compliance accordingly. Works with Information Technology to ensure that applicable ERP modules are updated, tested and functioning as intended. Financial Planning and Reporting Maintains accounting control over all of the university’s financial accounts and ensures the integrity of financial data. Prepares the university’s annual financial statements in accordance with GAAP . Meets external reporting requirements and deadlines, including but not limited to, those mandated by federal and state regulations, the IPEDS Survey and the Board of Trustees. Works with the Budget Office to develop annual budgets and calculate and negotiate the university’s F&A and fringe benefit rates. Oversees the annual audit and serves as the point of contact for any institutional audit. Provides ad hoc analysis and reporting. Leadership and Strategic Vision Fosters a culture of customer service and high standards of care. Prepares long-range financial, organizational and capital project plans and advises on their impacts. May serve as delegated authority to liaise with trustees, government and other external entities to perform relationship management and enhance data flow and communication. Stakeholder Engagement and Relationship Building Understands the needs of key customers and provides them with the financial and procedural information that allows them to make informed decisions and achieve their financial, strategic and operational goals. Ensures a customer-service-oriented billing and collection system for student accounts and deposit system for all university cash. Develops training for internal customers related to accounting and budget systems. Travel/Overtime Requirements Telecommuting Employees are not eligible for telecommuting/remote work during their 12-month probationary period. After that time, certain positions may be eligible for telecommuting/remote work at the discretion of the supervisor and in accordance with Winthrop policies. License/Certification CPA preferred. Type of Position Unclassified Position Status Full-Time FLSA Status Exempt Hours Per Week 37.5 Months per Year 12 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2027029S Open Date 09/16/2026 Close Date 09/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants PLEASE NOTE * A resume will not be reviewed to determine whether an applicant meets the qualifications outlined in the job vacancy notice (posting). * Responses to supplemental questions are considered part of the application; failure to respond will result in disqualification. NOTICE Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Given the qualifications and requirements outlined in the vacancy notice, list your relevant skills and experience. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your supervisory experience, including the number of direct reports, and summarize your management style. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22888": {
      "title": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Faculty, Human Resources Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct Faculty, Human Resources Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and until position is filled. Successful applications should include: 1. Curriculum vitae 2. Graduate and undergraduate transcripts. (Unofficial transcripts are acceptable for the application; official transcripts will be required later for an offer of employment.) For more information, please contact: Dr. Joanna Jackson, Chair Department of Management and Marketing Winthrop University jacksonj@winthrop.edu Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Human Resources Management Job Description The Department of Management & Marketing in Winthrop University’s College of Business and Technology invites applications for an Adjunct Faculty member to teach MGMT 323: Acquiring Talent . MGMT 323 introduces students to the talent acquisition process within organizations, including recruitment, selection, and compensation and benefits as they relate to attracting and acquiring talent. The course emphasizes the application of human resource management concepts to contemporary organizational practices. The ideal candidate will bring relevant academic and/or professional experience in human resources, talent acquisition, recruitment, or a related management field and demonstrate a commitment to engaging, student-centered instruction. Position Responsibilities Teach MGMT 323: Acquiring Talent in accordance with established course objectives and departmental expectations. Provide engaging, student-centered instruction on recruitment, selection, talent acquisition, and related compensation and benefits topics. Connect course concepts to current human resource management practices and real-world organizational challenges. Develop and deliver course materials, assignments, assessments, and learning activities that support achievement of course learning outcomes. Incorporate relevant professional examples, applied activities, and contemporary HR practices into the course when appropriate. Provide timely and constructive feedback to students and maintain appropriate communication with students throughout the semester. Maintain accurate course records and submit grades and other required materials in accordance with University policies and deadlines. Collaborate with the Department of Management & Marketing to ensure consistency with program and curricular expectations. About the College To learn more about the College of Business & Technology please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cbt/ . About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,200-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Not applicable Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 01/01/2027 Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Human Resources, Management, Business Administration, or a closely related field from an accredited institution Demonstrated knowledge of human resource management principles and practices, particularly in talent acquisition, recruitment, selection, and related areas. Ability to effectively teach and engage undergraduate students. Commitment to student learning and success. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience in human resources, talent acquisition, recruiting, selection, or a related area. Prior experience teaching at the college or university level. Professional HR certification, such as SHRM -CP, SHRM - SCP , PHR , or SPHR . Experience applying contemporary talent acquisition practices and technologies in an organizational setting. Experience incorporating real-world examples, cases, or applied learning activities into instruction. Demonstrated ability to engage and mentor undergraduate students. Employment Conditions Position is part-time, non-tenure-track, adjunct. Application Instructions Applications will be reviewed as they are received and until position is filled. Successful applications should include: 1. Curriculum vitae 2. Graduate and undergraduate transcripts. (Unofficial transcripts are acceptable for the application; official transcripts will be required later for an offer of employment.) For more information, please contact: Dr. Joanna Jackson, Chair Department of Management and Marketing Winthrop University jacksonj@winthrop.edu Open Date 09/11/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0015P PositionType: Adjunct Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
