    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22904": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Computer Science",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Computer Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant Professor, Computer Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The application review process begins November 1, 2026. Materials received after this date may be considered if an acceptable candidate has not been found. Applicants must submit the following materials electronically: Required Materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) including the names, phone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references from whom recommendation letters can be requested. Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research interests Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment) Evidence of excellence in teaching (e.g., course evaluations) Three letters of recommendation will be requested from semifinalists at a later date. (The CV must include the names, phone numbers, and email addresses for all references.) For questions about the position, please contact: R. Paul Wiegand Department of Computing & Information Sciences Winthrop University Rock Hill, SC 29733 803.323.4824 wiegandrp@winthrop.edu < mailto:wiegandrp@winthrop.edu > Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Assistant Professor, Computer Science Job Description The Department of Computing & Information Sciences at Winthrop University is seeking to fill two full-time, tenure-track faculty vacancies at the assistant professor level starting in Fall 2027. Successful candidates will join a collegial, teaching-focused environment that serves six different computing-oriented degree programs, including traditional ABET -accredited computer science, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, web development, computing information systems, and software engineering. Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong commitment to student learning and development, as well as the ability to engage in active scholarship in their fields. We are looking for education-focused individuals with a broad background in computer science and the ability to teach a variety of computing courses. Candidates with backgrounds in software engineering or web development are of interest for at least one position, though all interested candidates with strong general computer science backgrounds are encouraged to apply. Position Responsibilities Teach/develop courses in computer science and support the curriculum of our six computing degree programs for approximately 9 credits per semester. Advising and mentoring of students in computing degree programs. Conduct scholarly activities (e.g., research) in the field of specialization. Active engagement in student-centered activities (e.g., research) in the field of specialization. Engage in service to the department, college, university, discipline, and community. Participate in the Winthrop community as a scholarly academic. Other duties as assigned by the department chair. About the College To learn more about the College of Business & Technology please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cbt/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,200-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits At Winthrop University, we are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package that significantly enhances the total compensation for our employees. In partnership with the State of South Carolina and the Public Employee Benefit Authority ( PEBA ), our benefits include health and life insurance, generous paid leave, parental leave, and retirement programs. These benefits reflect our commitment to supporting the well-being and financial security of our employees. For more information please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/hr/employee-benefits.aspx . Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2027 Required Qualifications Ph.D. in computer science or strongly related field. Evidence of teaching effectiveness and strong commitment to student learning and development, including interest in undergraduate research. Evidence of an ability to maintain an active scholarship agenda. Evidence of strong interpersonal skills and the ability to mentor students. Preferred Qualifications Candidates with experience and interest in software engineering or web development will be preferred for at least one position, though all interested candidates with strong general backgrounds in computing programs are encouraged to apply. Employment Conditions This is a full-time, tenure-track appointment requiring daily on-campus contact; instructional duties during the academic year (9 months, Aug. 16 – May 15) Application Instructions The application review process begins November 1, 2026. Materials received after this date may be considered if an acceptable candidate has not been found. Applicants must submit the following materials electronically: Required Materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) including the names, phone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references from whom recommendation letters can be requested. Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research interests Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment) Evidence of excellence in teaching (e.g., course evaluations) Three letters of recommendation will be requested from semifinalists at a later date. (The CV must include the names, phone numbers, and email addresses for all references.) For questions about the position, please contact: R. Paul Wiegand Department of Computing & Information Sciences Winthrop University Rock Hill, SC 29733 803.323.4824 wiegandrp@winthrop.edu < mailto:wiegandrp@winthrop.edu > Open Date Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0022P Faculty Position Type Faculty Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty - Statement of Teaching Philosophy Faculty - Statement of Research Interests Faculty-All transcripts Faculty-Evidence of teaching excellence Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22907": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Marketing",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Marketing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant Professor, Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications should include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment). List of references Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research interests Priority will be given to applications received by October 18, 2026, but the position will be held open until filled. For questions about the position, please contact: Dr. Joanna Jackson, department chair, jacksonj@winthrop.edu. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Assistant Professor, Marketing Job Description The Department of Management & Marketing in Winthrop University’s AACSB -Accredited College of Business and Technology invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position in Marketing at the rank of Assistant Professor. We seek an enthusiastic, student-centered educator who is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service, and is eager to contribute to the continued growth and strategic direction of the department. The successful candidate will join a collaborative department focused on preparing students for meaningful careers through engaging instruction, experiential learning, strong connections with employers and alumni, and an innovative and relevant curriculum. The ideal candidate will bring energy and creativity to the classroom while also helping advance the department’s strategic priorities in career readiness, enrollment and program growth, curriculum innovation, community engagement, and program visibility. We especially value faculty who are interested in connecting classroom learning with professional practice and helping students develop the skills needed to succeed in a rapidly changing business environment. Position Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in marketing data analytics, marketing research and possibly sales while delivering high-quality, engaging, and student-centered instruction. Maintain an active scholarly agenda in Marketing consistent with the expectations for tenure and promotion at Winthrop University. Create a supportive learning environment that promotes student engagement, academic success, professional development, and career readiness. Incorporate contemporary business practices, emerging technologies, and innovative teaching approaches into the curriculum, including appropriate applications of artificial intelligence and other evolving technologies. Support experiential and applied learning opportunities that connect academic content with real-world business challenges. Advise and mentor students regarding academic progress, career preparation, internships, and professional opportunities. Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous improvement to ensure Marketing programs remain relevant, innovative, and responsive to student and employer needs. Participate in student recruitment, retention, and enrollment-growth initiatives for Marketing and other departmental programs. Help strengthen relationships with alumni, employers, community organizations, and other external partners to expand opportunities for students. Contribute to departmental efforts to increase the visibility and recognition of Marketing programs, faculty, students, and alumni. Participate actively in the collaborative work of the Department of Management & Marketing and contribute to departmental, college, and university service. Support the department’s strategic vision and contribute to initiatives that advance career readiness, enrollment, curriculum innovation, community engagement, and program visibility. About the College To learn more about the College of Business & Technology please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cbt/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,200-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits At Winthrop University, we are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package that significantly enhances the total compensation for our employees. In partnership with the State of South Carolina and the Public Employee Benefit Authority ( PEBA ), our benefits include health and life insurance, generous paid leave, parental leave, and retirement programs. These benefits reflect our commitment to supporting the well-being and financial security of our employees. For more information please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/hr/employee-benefits.aspx . Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2027 Required Qualifications Ph.D., DBA , or terminal degree in Marketing or a closely related field from an accredited institution. ABD candidates who will complete their degree by the position start date may be considered. Previous experience in undergraduate or graduate-level teaching in data analytics, marketing research, or other quantitative courses in marketing. Demonstrated potential to maintain a scholarly agenda appropriate for a tenure-track faculty appointment. Ability to build and maintain professional relationships with employers, industry partners, and community organizations. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of highly effective, engaging, and innovative undergraduate and graduate-level teaching. Professional or applied experience in Marketing or a related business field. Experience incorporating experiential learning, emerging technologies, artificial intelligence, or other innovative practices into teaching. Experience developing relationships with employers, alumni, community organizations, or other external partners. Experience supporting student recruitment, retention, career readiness, or professional development initiatives. Interest in contributing to curriculum innovation and the growth and visibility of academic programs. Interest in creating and teaching courses in professional selling. Employment Conditions This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure track faculty appointment. Application Instructions Applications should include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment). List of references Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research interests Priority will be given to applications received by October 18, 2026, but the position will be held open until filled. For questions about the position, please contact: Dr. Joanna Jackson, department chair, jacksonj@winthrop.edu. Open Date 09/18/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0023P Faculty Position Type Faculty Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All transcripts Faculty - List of References Faculty - Statement of Teaching Philosophy Faculty - Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22915": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Exercise Science",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Exercise Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant Professor, Exercise Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application review will begin on October 30, 2026. Applications received after the start of review may be considered if an acceptable candidate is not identified. Applications should include: A cover letter including the candidate’s interest in the position, qualifications, leadership experience, teaching philosophy, and research interests is required. Curriculum vitae (CV) including the names, phone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references from whom recommendation letters can be requested. Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment). Copy of CSCS credential Additional materials may be requested during the review process. Three letters of recommendation will be requested from semifinalists at a later date. (The CV must include the names, phone numbers, and email addresses for all references.) Applications received after the start of review may be considered if an acceptable candidate is not identified. Specific questions related to this search should be directed to Dr. Janet Wojcik at wojcikj@winthrop.edu. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Assistant Professor, Exercise Science Job Description The Department of Physical Education, Sport, and Human Performance ( PESH ) at Winthrop University is seeking an innovative and involved tenure-track assistant professor to serve as Internship and Field Experience Coordinator and teach in an established Bachelor of Science in Exercise Science program. The program is accredited by the Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs ( CAAHEP ) and the Commission on Accreditation of Exercise Science (CoAES). The program will be seeking accreditation with Council on Accreditation of Strength and Conditioning Education ( CASCE ). The individual will collaborate with other faculty to ensure that undergraduate students interested in pursuing exercise science receive high-quality didactic education and exceptional internship and field experiences. We seek a candidate who will be an exemplary leader, teacher, scholar, and active participant in the college, on campus, with community partners, and in professional organizations. Position Responsibilities Serve as the Internship and Field Experience Coordinator for the Exercise Science program; Maintain comprehensive records of student internship and field experiences; Teach courses in exercise science, strength and conditioning, health, and other related fields at the undergraduate and graduate levels; Support the vision for program initiatives, curriculum development, and accreditation; Serve as a productive faculty member in all areas of university expectations (student intellectual development, scholarly activity, professional stewardship, and academic responsibility); Actively engage in student recruitment and selection processes; Advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students; Foster collaborative relationships with sport, allied health, and other organizations to develop internship and field experience placements and opportunities for collaborative service to the profession; Use technology to enhance student learning, increase access, maintain program data, and facilitate recruitment and retention efforts; and Engage in teaching and other program-related activities in the evenings, online, and occasional weekends, as needed. About the College To learn more about the Richard W. Riley College of Education, Sport, and Human Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/ceshs/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,200-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits At Winthrop University, we are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package that significantly enhances the total compensation for our employees. In partnership with the State of South Carolina and the Public Employee Benefit Authority ( PEBA ), our benefits include health and life insurance, generous paid leave, parental leave, and retirement programs. These benefits reflect our commitment to supporting the well-being and financial security of our employees. For more information please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/hr/employee-benefits.aspx . Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2027 Required Qualifications Doctorate with specialization in exercise science, strength and conditioning or closely related field ( ABD with completion by summer 2027 will be considered); Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist ( CSCS ) credential; Experience as a provider of exercise science or strength and conditioning services to clients or patients; Foundation for successful collegiate teaching; Foundation for active scholarship; and Ability to work collaboratively with departmental and other university members Preferred Qualifications Experience with CASCE and/or CoAES accreditation procedures; Experience supervising exercise science or strength and conditioning internship and field experiences; Demonstrated ability in the use of technology and online learning for instructional purposes; Demonstrated ability to use technology for student record keeping and management; Experience working with underrepresented students and students from at-risk backgrounds; and Expertise in one or more of the following areas of exercise science or strength and conditioning: exercise physiology, biomechanics, kinesiology, exercise prescription, athlete assessment and performance, and military and tactical athlete performance. Employment Conditions Position is full-time, nine-month, tenure-track with the possibility of summer employment. Salary is commensurate with qualifications. Application Instructions Application review will begin on October 30, 2026. Applications received after the start of review may be considered if an acceptable candidate is not identified. Applications should include: A cover letter including the candidate’s interest in the position, qualifications, leadership experience, teaching philosophy, and research interests is required. Curriculum vitae (CV) including the names, phone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references from whom recommendation letters can be requested. Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment). Copy of CSCS credential Additional materials may be requested during the review process. Three letters of recommendation will be requested from semifinalists at a later date. (The CV must include the names, phone numbers, and email addresses for all references.) Applications received after the start of review may be considered if an acceptable candidate is not identified. Specific questions related to this search should be directed to Dr. Janet Wojcik at wojcikj@winthrop.edu. Open Date 09/23/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0024P Faculty Position Type Faculty Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All transcripts License or Certificate Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22897": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Art History",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Art History Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct Instructor, Art History Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Please send the following required materials: Cover Letter Current Curriculum Vitae (CV). Transcripts (Unofficial documents can support the application. Official transcripts are required for the appointment) Contact information for two professional references. Questions about the position may be directed to Prof. Mark Hamilton, Chair of the Department of Fine Arts (hamiltonm@winthrop.edu). Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct Instructor, Art History Job Description The Department of Fine Arts at Winthrop University is seeking applications for a part-time adjunct position with the expertise needed to serve as an Instructor of Art History. The ideal candidate will be a dedicated and experienced individual who can teach introductory courses in art history, specifically ARTH 175: Introduction to Ancient and Medieval Art (in person; for majors and non-majors). Position Responsibilities Adjunct faculty, part-time appointments, are expected to adhere to all policies and procedures expected of university employees. Adjunct faculty will: Offer evidence of effective Student Intellectual Development activities Demonstrate a commitment to meeting the academic responsibility requirements for all faculty (e.g., adherence to academic policies, participating in the collection of assessment data necessary for course and program evaluation). Attend any College orientation sessions. Develop and distribute a written course syllabus as outlined by university policy and College policy at the first course meeting. Present course content as announced to students and as approved by the faculty. Meet all assigned classes or make appropriate alternative arrangements for the class when an absence is unavoidable. Schedule and maintain regular office hours (in-person or virtual) and be available to students. Award academic credit based on the professional evaluation of academic performance. Observe the policies and procedures of the department, College, and the University. Administer student evaluations and any additional assessment instruments required by the University. File an annual report that provides evidence of progress and involvement that is responsive to feedback and meets expectations of rank. About the College To learn more about the College of Visual & Performing Arts please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cvpa/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,200-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Not applicable Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 01/01/2027 Required Qualifications Successful candidates must have a master’s degree and a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in art history. Preferred Qualifications MA or PhD in art history. Previous experience teaching undergraduate students and proficiency with instructional technology and Learning Management Systems (e.g., Canvas, Blackboard) are preferred. Employment Conditions Position is part-time, adjunct, non-tenure track Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue throughout the 2026-27 academic year. Please send the following required materials: Cover Letter Current Curriculum Vitae (CV). Transcripts (Unofficial documents can support the application. Official transcripts are required for the appointment) Contact information for two professional references. Questions about the position may be directed to Prof. Mark Hamilton, Chair of the Department of Fine Arts (hamiltonm@winthrop.edu). Open Date 09/18/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0020P Faculty Position Type Adjunct Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty-All transcripts Faculty - List of References Optional Documents Media File Portfolio IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22905": {
      "title": "Assistant and Associate Professor, Athletic Training",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Assistant and Associate Professor, Athletic Training Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Assistant and Associate Professor, Athletic Training Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application review will begin on October 30, 2026. Applications received after the start of review may be considered if an acceptable candidate is not identified. Applications should include: Cover letter including the candidate’s interest in the position, desired rank, interest in clinical experience leadership role, applicable qualifications, and leadership experience. Curriculum vitae (CV) including the names, phone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references from whom recommendation letters can be requested. Detailed statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests; Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment). Three letters of recommendation will be requested from semifinalists at a later date. (The CV must include the names, phone numbers, and email addresses for all references.) Additional materials may be requested during the review process. Specific questions related to this search should be directed to Dr. Alice McLaine at mclainea@winthrop.edu . Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Assistant and Associate Professor, Athletic Training Job Description The Department of Physical Education, Sport, and Human Performance ( PESH ) at Winthrop University is seeking two faculty in Athletic Training. Through this search we seek innovative and engaged tenure-track faculty. One position is at the associate professor rank and the second is at the assistant professor rank. Both faculty will teach in an established and evolving Master of Science in Athletic Training program. One position will include the Director of Clinical Education responsibilities. The program is accredited by the Commission on Accreditation of Athletic Training Education ( CAATE ). The individuals will collaborate with other faculty to ensure that graduate students and undergraduate students interested in pursuing athletic training receive high-quality didactic education, practice remains congruent with disciplinary standards, and clinical experiences meet the needs of health care professionals in training. We seek candidates who will be exemplary leaders, teachers, scholars, and active participants in the college, on campus, with community partners, and professional organizations. Position Responsibilities Teach courses in athletic training, exercise science, and health at the graduate and undergraduate levels; Contribute to program initiatives, curriculum development, and accreditation; Serve as a productive faculty member in all areas of university expectations (student intellectual development, scholarly activity, professional stewardship, and academic responsibility); Lead efforts to develop and maintain strong cohorts, including recruitment and selection processes; Advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students; Foster collaborative relationships with medical and sport organizations to develop clinical experience placements and opportunities for service to the profession.; Use technology to enhance student learning, increase access, maintain program data, and facilitate recruitment and retention efforts; and Engage in teaching and other program-related activities in the evenings, summers (this is a 12-month program), online, and occasional weekends, as needed. About the College To learn more about the Richard W. Riley College of Education, Sport, and Human Sciences please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/ceshs/ . About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 5,200-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits At Winthrop University, we are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package that significantly enhances the total compensation for our employees. In partnership with the State of South Carolina and the Public Employee Benefit Authority ( PEBA ), our benefits include health and life insurance, generous paid leave, parental leave, and retirement programs. These benefits reflect our commitment to supporting the well-being and financial security of our employees. For more information please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/hr/employee-benefits.aspx . Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 08/16/2027 Required Qualifications Doctorate with specialization in athletic training or closely related field ( ABD with completion by summer 2027 will be considered); Current Board of Certification ( BOC ) credential; Eligible for licensure as an athletic trainer in South Carolina; Experience as a provider of athletic training services to scholastic, intercollegiate, or professional athletes or other clinical sites; Record of successful collegiate teaching (required for associate rank and desired for assistant rank); Record of scholarly / creative work (required for associate rank and foundation to develop record is required at the assistant rank); Ability to work collaboratively with department colleagues and other members of the university community Preferred Qualifications Experience with CAATE accreditation procedures; Previous experience teaching in a CAATE -accredited program; Experience supervising and/or establishing athletic training clinical experiences; Demonstrated ability in the use of simulation, technology, and online learning for instructional purposes; Demonstrated ability to use technology for student record keeping and management; Experience working with underrepresented students and students from at-risk backgrounds; Expertise in one or more of the following areas: evidence-based practice, therapeutic interventions, administration, research and writing, and the implementation of standardized patients for instructional purposes. Employment Conditions The positions are full-time, nine-month, tenure-track with an expectation of summer employment paid based on credits taught and enrollment. The nine-month salary is commensurate with qualifications and rank. Application Instructions Application review will begin on October 30, 2026. Applications received after the start of review may be considered if an acceptable candidate is not identified. Applications should include: Cover letter including the candidate’s interest in the position, desired rank, interest in clinical experience leadership role, applicable qualifications, and leadership experience. Curriculum vitae (CV) including the names, phone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references from whom recommendation letters can be requested. Detailed statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests; Graduate degree transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable for application but official transcripts will be required for an offer of employment). Three letters of recommendation will be requested from semifinalists at a later date. (The CV must include the names, phone numbers, and email addresses for all references.) Additional materials may be requested during the review process. Specific questions related to this search should be directed to Dr. Alice McLaine at mclainea@winthrop.edu . Open Date 09/23/2026 Application Review Date 10/30/2026 Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0021P Faculty Position Type Faculty Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Faculty - Statement of Teaching Philosophy Faculty - Statement of Research Interests Faculty-All transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22912": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Piano Instructor",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Adjunct, Piano Instructor – Collaborative and Applied Lessons Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Adjunct, Piano Instructor – Collaborative and Applied Lessons Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applicants will begin on August 12, 2026 and continues until the position is filled. For more information, please email Lorrie Crochet at crochetl@winthrop.edu. Position Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Adjunct, Piano Instructor – Collaborative and Applied Lessons Job Description Collaborative pianist during rehearsals and performances for ensemble and soloists in the Department of Music. Instructor for applied piano lessons as assigned. Position Responsibilities Serve the Department of Music as a collaborative pianist for ensemble and solo rehearsals and performances. Teach applied piano lessons as assigned. About the College To learn more about the College of Visual & Performing Arts please visit: https://www.winthrop.edu/cvpa/ About Winthrop University Founded in 1886, Winthrop University in Rock Hill, South Carolina, offers its 6,000-plus undergraduate and graduate students an educational experience that blends liberal arts, professional programs, global awareness, and civic engagement. In its colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business and Technology; Education, Sport, and Human Sciences; and Visual and Performing Arts, Winthrop embraces only those programs and activities that can be delivered at an exemplary level. Winthrop University is achieving national stature as a competitive and distinctive co-educational, public, residential, comprehensive, values-oriented institution. The values of service, excellence, community, and leadership provide the foundation for Winthrop’s continuing development and shape Winthrop’s continuing success. Numerous national accolades reflect the sustained high quality and value of the Winthrop Experience, including the most recent U.S. News & World Report ’s ranking of Winthrop as one of the top-10 public comprehensive universities in the South. Winthrop is an active member of the Rock Hill community and recognized as a key component of the region’s economic resurgence. Approximately 20 minutes from Charlotte, North Carolina, Winthrop has direct access to and is engaged in a broad and expansive regional business community. Winthrop’s beautiful campus encompasses a rich architectural blend of neo-Georgian buildings and is included in the National Register of Historic Places. The attractive recreational and research complex area that surrounds Winthrop Lake is home to Winthrop’s 18 Division I men’s and women’s sports. Benefits Not applicable Background Check Winthrop University is committed to providing a safe campus community. Winthrop conducts background investigations for applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial (credit) report or driving history check. Position Availability 09/23/2026 Required Qualifications Master of Music in Piano Performance Experience as a collaborative pianist Experience teaching private piano lessons Preferred Qualifications Proficiency with Microsoft Office and Google Docs Employment Conditions Position is non-tenure track, adjunct Application Instructions Review of applicants will begin on August 12, 2026 and continues until the position is filled. For more information, please email Lorrie Crochet at crochetl@winthrop.edu. Open Date 09/23/2026 Application Review Date Close Date Posting Number 2027FC0007P Faculty Position Type Adjunct Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Faculty-All transcripts Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://winthrop.peopleadmin.com/postings/22939": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Office of Grants and Sponsored Research Development (GSRD)",
      "description": "Winthrop University Applicant Portal | Executive Director, Office of Grants and Sponsored Research Development (GSRD) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Executive Director, Office of Grants and Sponsored Research Development (GSRD) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Three professional references, including contact information, are required in the reference section on the application. Posting Details Position Information Winthrop Position Title Executive Director, Office of Grants and Sponsored Research Development (GSRD) State Title Director State Class Code UP03 State Pay Table Annual Salary/Hiring Range $94,929 to $100,000; actual salary depends on qualifications. Job Purpose The Executive Director for the Office of Grants and Sponsored Research Development ( GSRD ) manages and optimizes all aspects of the university’s grants and contracts administration, including office operations, pre-award and compliance personnel, proposal development and submission processes and research compliance, and provides grant administration support services to faculty, staff and students in pursuit of internal and external funding for research, creative activity and program development. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in business, public administration, research discipline, social science or other appropriate field. At least five years of progressively responsible experience in research administration at an institution of higher education with in-depth knowledge of grant administration (pre- and post-award) practices, processes and procedures. Preferred Qualifications Ten or more years of progressively responsible experience in research administration at an institution of higher education with in-depth knowledge of grant administration practices (pre- and post-award), processes and procedures. Experience with Grants.gov, NSF FastLane/Research. gov, eRA Commons and other online grant submission portals. Demonstrated commitment to the values of diversity, equity and inclusion within higher education. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Summary Working knowledge of non-financial compliance management (i.e., IRB , IACUC , IBC ). Comprehensive knowledge of federal (e.g. NSF , NIH or ED) regulations and grants/contracts management guidelines (i.e., OMB Uniform Guidance 2 CFR 200). Working knowledge of Grants.gov, NSF FastLane/Research. gov, eRA Commons and other online grant submission portals. Excellent written communication as well as editing and proofreading skills and ability to generate high-quality written communications, grants and reports. Attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to communicate and collaborate with diverse groups and personnel across campus as well as sponsor representatives. Strong financial, audit and computer skills. Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to facilitate application submissions while effectively managing different personalities and following guidelines and policies. Ability to manage multiple and competing priorities and deadlines. Ability to design and conduct professional development trainings. Ability to work independently, analyze situations quickly and accurately and formulate effective courses of action. Job Summary Pre-Award Administration Develops proposal budgets and writes budget justifications. Reviews all grant applications to ensure compliance with university policies and procedures, State of South Carolina laws, federal regulations and sponsor guidelines. Ensures applications are formatted, packaged and submitted according to sponsor requirements. Oversees grant application processing, electronic approvals, records maintenance and proposal tracking in university systems. Serves as an Authorized Organizational Representative to submit and administer all federal grant applications and signs official grant documents on behalf of the university. Serves as liaison to funding agencies to resolve questions or challenges that arise during research development and pre-award processes. Reviews and processes grant and contract awards, ensuring accuracy and compliance while coordinating award setup and tracking within university financial systems. Reviews and coordinates all award modifications and grant extension requests, working with sponsors to obtain award amendments. Prepares, administers and approves all subawards with partner institutions and sponsors. Serves on the Research Council, reads and scores all applications, participates in application review sessions and makes funding recommendations to the Provost. Research Development Identifies potential funding opportunities and cultivates a portfolio of federal, state and local sponsors, companies and foundations to support research, training, creative activity, professional and program development and institutional infrastructure needs. Disseminates to the campus community regularly. Meets, collaborates and stays engaged with members of the campus community to discuss and remain aware of their research, creative and programmatic interests and funding needs. Provides technical assistance to faculty and staff by designing and presenting research development and pre-award administration training activities that cultivate interest and increase knowledge and skills. Assists faculty and staff in the development of competitive proposals to external funding agencies and fosters an environment that supports the campus community’s pursuit of external funding. Assists in writing grant applications as needed. Administrative and Operational Provides leadership to and managerial oversight of Grants Office staff and operations to ensure a high level of service to the campus community. Supervises the Compliance Coordinator, who is responsible for administering the Institutional Research Board ( IRB ), Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee ( IACUC ), and Biosafety Committee. Completes GSRD’s annual Continuous Improvement Report and Plan. Updates website content as needed. Develops and maintains GSRD operational procedures. Writes and updates guides and handbooks. Supports internal committees to ensure compliance with rules and policies for research occurring on campus. Compiles proposal data and provides periodic reports to the Provost, Deans and Board of Trustees. Generates effort reports quarterly. Hires and trains staff. Travel/Overtime Requirements Occasional overtime may be required to meet deadlines. Telecommuting Employees are not eligible for telecommuting/remote work during their 12-month probationary period. After that time, certain positions may be eligible for telecommuting/remote work at the discretion of the supervisor and in accordance with Winthrop policies. License/Certification Type of Position Unclassified Position Status Full-Time FLSA Status Exempt Hours Per Week 37.5 Months per Year 12 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2027030S Open Date 09/23/2026 Close Date 11/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Three professional references, including contact information, are required in the reference section on the application. PLEASE NOTE * A resume will not be reviewed to determine whether an applicant meets the qualifications outlined in the job vacancy notice (posting). * Responses to supplemental questions are considered part of the application; failure to respond will result in disqualification. NOTICE Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Describe your experience working directly with faculty, researchers, administrators or external sponsors to develop and advance funding opportunities. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experience administering grant awards, including award review, setup, modifications, extensions and subawards. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents IN THE HEART OF THE CAROLINAS © Winthrop University · 701 Oakland Avenue · Rock Hill, SC 29733, USA · 803/323-2211 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
